ng in billions of dollars in  tariffs I love the position that we are  in we've gone up a lot since our great  election  it means for a country to go up a lot is  is very dumb and childish and stupid but  the fundamental misunderstanding is that  China doesn't pay the tariffs the money  that Trump is talking about taking in is  coming from American companies and  American people who are paying the  tariffs this is a dangerous man who  doesn't understand fundamentally basic  things this is weaponized ignorant  stocks are crashing trump's ad chair  trump adds to tariffs to china china  adds tariffs Trump adds more tariffs and  then the whole circle sort of starts  again and again and meanwhile China  forges other relationships while our  companies and our people get screwed so  I'm gonna try another approach on this  today because there's lots of people who  are apparently as confused as Trump is  on this issue because I get emails from  people saying David you're against  tariff so you're a pro free-trade guy  free trades been a disaster for hundreds  of millions of people on this planet you  can't possibly be for free trade can you  David every single email I get that  attempts to make that economic analysis  forgets that countries don't exist in an  echo chamber the world didn't start in  2019 or 2018 if we were just starting  nation-states and setting up countries  today and economics and economies more  importantly didn't already have hundreds  of years of track records it would be a  philosophical debate over free trade vs.  protectionism and that philosophical  debate would have practical implications  that's not the reality right now we are  mostly engaged in a battle over  principles of free trade versus  protectionism that are only relevant in  the theoretical and sort of  philosophical world where countries  haven't existed for hundreds of years in  the real world we have 200 years almost  200 years of industrialization and  specialization so the way that T